<% content_for :title, "OpenClaw on Sabha — Open Source AI Assistant for Communities" %>
<% content_for :meta_description, "Run an AI assistant — OpenAI, Anthropic, or local LLMs — inside Sabha rooms and DMs. Open source, self-hosted, no webhook URL needed." %>

<div class="landing">

<%= render "shared/marketing_header" %>

<%# ═══════════════════════════════════ OPENCLAW ═══════════════════════════════════ %>
<section class="landing-section" style="padding-top: 6rem;">
  <div class="landing-inner" style="max-width: 680px;">
    <div class="landing-section-header" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; gap: 1.25rem;">
      <%= image_tag "logos/openclaw-claw.svg", alt: "OpenClaw", width: 56, height: 56 %>
      <span class="landing-label">INTEGRATION</span>
      <h1 class="landing-section-title" style="margin: 0;">OpenClaw on Sabha</h1>
    </div>

    <div style="margin: 2.5rem 0;">
      <%= render "saas/landing/feature_video", src: "screenshots/bot-sabha.mp4", poster: "screenshots/bot-sabha-poster.webp", width: 1280, height: 720, label: "An OpenClaw AI agent in a Sabha room" %>
    </div>

    <div style="font-size: 1.125rem; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--color-text-secondary, #555);">
      <p>Sabha provides first-class <a href="https://openclaw.ai" target="_blank" class="landing-link">OpenClaw</a> support over WebSockets. The AI bot connects outbound to your workspace — no webhook URL to configure, no public IP to expose, no tunnels. Self-hosted Sabha and Sabha Cloud both work.</p>

      <p style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">@mention it in any room, or DM it directly, and it replies — powered by the LLM of your choice (OpenAI, Anthropic, or a local model).</p>

      <p style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">No third-party chat dependency, no third-party AI dependency. OpenClaw runs on Discord, Telegram, Slack, and a dozen other channels — but with Sabha you can self-host the entire stack. Your community, your bot, your data, your servers.</p>

      <h3 style="margin-top: 3rem; font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--color-text-primary, #111);">How it works</h3>

      <ol style="margin-top: 1rem; padding-left: 1.25rem;">
        <li style="margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">Install the plugin: <code style="background: var(--color-bg-subtle, #f4f4f4); padding: 0.15rem 0.4rem; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.95em;">openclaw plugins install @sabha-co/openclaw-sabha</code></li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">Run <code style="background: var(--color-bg-subtle, #f4f4f4); padding: 0.15rem 0.4rem; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.95em;">openclaw configure --section channels</code> and paste a Sabha join URL.</li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">@mention the bot in any room, or DM it directly. It's that quiet.</li>
      </ol>

      <h3 style="margin-top: 3rem; font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--color-text-primary, #111);">What the AI can do</h3>

      <p style="margin-top: 1rem;">Rooms, threads, DMs, reactions, attachments, search — the AI speaks Sabha natively. Give it MCP tools, RAG over your community's docs, vision on uploaded images, voice — anything OpenClaw skills support. In rooms it only replies when @mentioned, so it stays out of the way. In DMs it's always listening.</p>

      <h3 style="margin-top: 3rem; font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--color-text-primary, #111);">Get started</h3>

      <ul style="margin-top: 1rem; list-style: none; padding: 0;">
        <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;"><a href="https://github.com/sabha-co/openclaw-sabha" target="_blank" class="landing-link">Sabha plugin on GitHub</a></li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;"><a href="https://openclaw.ai" target="_blank" class="landing-link">OpenClaw homepage</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="landing-divider"></div>

<%= render "shared/marketing_footer" %>

</div>
